From e5f8e474463f775a8f9f81b7ec88a5a89e7dff7e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:27:31 -0500
Subject: [RFC PATCH 1/2] libmisc: Add rtems_backtrace()

RTEMS has no way for an application to obtain a backtrace.  Add
rtems_backtrace(), which stores the addresses of the frames of its
caller in an array, and rtems_backtrace_print(), which prints them with
printk() for offline symbolization with rtems-addr2line.

Both walk the stack with _Unwind_Backtrace() of libgcc, which reads the
DWARF call frame information of the .eh_frame sections.  The walk ends
at the first frame without call frame information.  RTEMS is built
without -funwind-tables, so a backtrace covers application code built
with unwind tables and ends where it enters RTEMS code.  Build
backtrace.c itself with -funwind-tables, since the walk starts in it.

Each address is in the call instruction, not at the return address, so
that it resolves to the line of the call.  For a frame entered from an
interrupt or exception, which the call frame information marks as a
signal frame, it is the interrupted instruction.

Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
